{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310527,"nonce":"UTvdbTeYeER/lLwiEn8/xJifpXE=","title":"2026-09-20 0a345d88/b978dcb9/d0a1e8ff (577-\u003e581) — select-based array bounds clamp cost nbody 11% (branch form fixed it); PtrAdd on i64 ...","message":"**nbody perf (user reported \"steadily loses to hxcpp\").** CI benchmarks:\nrayzor-llvm 703 vs cpp 729 through 84c057bf; 811 vs 727 at 6113ac5e; first\nlosing run = 30015d6b (the array-read OOB clamp). The clamp was two selects\n(address and loaded value) per element read — compare latency in front of\nevery load. Fix 0a345d88: `if idx \u003cu len { load } else null` via blocks +\nphi in `lower_index_access`. Local min-user-time A/B: unchecked 0.598s,\nselect 0.649, branch 0.605; a 4M sum loop 0.353/0.383/0.270 (branch is\nFASTER than unchecked). Verify on the next CI Benchmarks artifact\n(`gh run download \u003cid\u003e -p 'benchmark-results*'`, results_\u003cdate\u003e.json -\u003e\nname=nbody -\u003e results[].runtime_ms).\n\n**Also from the clamp:** `a[1][0]` on `Array\u003cArray\u003cInt\u003e\u003e` PANICKED the LLVM\nbackend since 30015d6b (PtrAdd on an IntValue: the inner `len` read). Load\nand Store coerce via `address_as_pointer`; PtrAdd now does too. LoadGlobal\nof an i32 handed back the zero-extended i64 → `a % b` on static Ints = 255\nunder `--llvm` (57634ab, fixed same commit).\n\n**Method values (d0a1e8ff):** bare `fn = inst` / `a.map(inst)` lowered to a\nFunctionRef of the closure adapter with a null env (SIGSEGV); now rewritten\nto `this.inst` in the Ident arm, guarded by `lowering_callee` so a call's\ncallee keeps its direct binding. `this.m.bind(x)` was also broken: the bind\nlowering only special-cased a Variable receiver; MethodReference receivers\nnow build a MethodCall, spelling `this` as the VARIABLE so the lambda\ncaptures it (a `This` node inside the generated lambda did not capture).\n\n**`this.m()` inside an abstract** resolved to the abstract's OWN method\n(Rest.toString recursed → silent death). Fixed ONLY for abstracts over\nbuilt-ins (no class symbol for `this_type`); over a class/interface the old\nbehaviour is load-bearing: `Map.set` → `this.set` binds to Map.set and the\nruntime-map rerouting keys on that; resolving on IMap made `copy`\nunresolvable. haxe.ds.Vector is broken at every arm (b048e0b, 36 corpus\nfiles); Map.copy() `can't resolve symbol copy` pre-existing (372fe01).\n\n**Array.toString** joined with \", \" — Haxe prints `[1,2,3]`. Maps keep\n`[k =\u003e v, k2 =\u003e v2]`. Shim aeq now structural (Std.string fallback) like\nupstream Assert.same.\n\n**Measurement traps hit today:** (1) a gate script running `LLVM=1 run.sh`\nfaked a 42-row regression — CI scores the DEFAULT tier; (2) a binary COPIED\nout of a worktree loses exe-relative haxe-std and behaves differently — run\nworktree builds in place; (3) the machine was shared with another session's\ncargo builds — use min of interleaved user-time, not means.\n\n**Excluding forward-ref stubs from `stdlib_function_name_map`** (attempt at\nTestRest 14ccff1) fixed TestRest but rebound Int64.toInt \u0026 co by bare name\n(TestInt64, Issue8845/8849/5289 LOST) — reverted; the real fix renumbers the\nnever-renumbered module's entries.\n\nRelated: [[bugs_rest_args_and_abstract_type_params]],\n[[bugs_conformance_scores_the_tiered_path_not_llvm]],\n[[feedback_conformance_must_use_in_repo_binary]],\n[[feedback_check_ci_benchmarks_after_typer_changes]].\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_array_clamp_regressed_nbody_and_method_values` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}